---
import LegalPage from "../../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../lib/site-config";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Accessibility Statement — LENZ"
  description="LENZ's accessibility statement — our approach to an accessible website, known limitations, and how to reach us about an issue."
  eyebrow="Accessibility"
  heading="Accessibility Statement"
  updated="September 11, 2026"
>
  <p>
    LENZ wants this website to be usable by as many people as possible, including people who use
    a keyboard instead of a mouse, a screen reader, voice control, or other assistive technology.
  </p>

  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <p>
    This site is built to align with the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at
    Level AA. That includes things like a logical heading structure, visible keyboard-focus
    indicators, labeled form fields with clear error messages, alt text on meaningful images,
    sufficient color contrast, and respecting your device's reduced-motion setting.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not claim this site is certified or guaranteed to meet every WCAG success criterion at
    all times. Accessibility is an ongoing effort, not a one-time checkbox — we review and improve
    it as the site changes.
  </p>

  <h2>Known limitations</h2>
  <p>
    We're not aware of any significant barriers at this time. If a specific piece of content —
    including an embedded video, a form, or the portfolio gallery — doesn't work well with the
    assistive technology you use, we want to know about it (see below).
  </p>

  <h2>What we've deliberately avoided</h2>
  <p>
    This site does not use an accessibility "overlay" plugin (a third-party widget that claims to
    automatically fix accessibility issues) and does not block right-click, text selection, or
    other normal browser behavior. Accessibility here is built into the site's actual markup and
    styling, not bolted on afterward.
  </p>

  <h2>Feedback</h2>
  <p>
    If you run into an accessibility barrier anywhere on this site, please let us know — including
    the page you were on and what happened — and we'll do our best to address it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contact.email}`}>{siteConfig.contact.email}</a>
  </p>
</LegalPage>
